Subject: [PATCH 14/14] amd64: bind (init-program)/(go) where $find can see them

Moves openbios_init() in arch/amd64/openbios.c to AFTER device_end(). One call
site; the ordering is the whole of it.

openbios_init() binds `(init-program)` and `(go)` with bind_func, which is
`is-cfunc` (libopenbios/clib.fs:17), which is `$create` -- and $create defines
into the CURRENT vocabulary. While a device context is still open, every word it
creates lands in that node rather than the dictionary, where $find cannot see it.

MEASURED, not reasoned. Markers were planted through arch_init and probed at the
prompt:

    bound as arch_init's first statement    MISSING
    bound straight after openbios_init()    MISSING
    bound after modules_init()              MISSING
    platform-boot, bound after device_end() FOUND

$find itself works (`dup`, `is-cfunc`, `(does>)` all found, and `(does>)` also
rules out "parenthesised names are unfindable"). bind_func works. The only thing
between the missing words and the found one is device_end().

The symptom was that `load` of ANY file ended in

    Unable to locate (init-program)!

from forth/debugging/client.fs:57 -- $load's last step -- so the entire
`load` client path was unreachable on amd64.

With the call moved, measured on the 64-bit firmware:

    0 > load /ide@1/cdrom@0:\marker.fth        -> clean, ok, empty stack
    0 > load-base load-size evaluate
    SPIKE-FORTH-LOADED

which is TODO 13.1's checkpoint -- "a .fth loaded off media prints its own
marker" -- met. PR #294 recorded that checkpoint as one that CANNOT be reached;
that was true of the code as it stood and is now false, and 13.1 says so.

NOT fixed by calling device_end() earlier instead. Tried: `set_property: NULL
phandle` and then a general protection fault at 08:0000000000102ba3, named by
Spike 2's handler, because the device tree is not built yet at the top of
arch_init. The call moves; the teardown stays where it is.

Control run and watched to bite: with openbios_init() put back before
device_end(), `(init-program)` and `(go)` are MISSING again and `load` prints
"Unable to locate (init-program)!" again. Restored, both are found.

Scope is deliberately arch/amd64 only. Three further defects on this path were
found and are NOT touched here, because they live in arch-neutral code shared
with x86, ppc and sparc, and changing them alters three targets this lab does
not test:

  2. `load-state >ls.file-size` is never set on the $load path -- `!load-size`
     writes a separate `variable file-size` (client.fs:37-41). Two records of one
     fact. Measured: load-base held the file while ls.file-size read 0.
  3. `eval2` (libopenbios/initprogram.c:152) is the ONLY reference to that name
     in the tree and NOTHING defines it. fword() on a missing word is silent, so
     the Forth-source loader has never evaluated a byte on any arch.
  4. even with 2 and 3 addressed locally, the `go` trampoline still evaluates
     nothing. UNKNOWN.

Those are why the recipe above uses `evaluate` directly rather than `go`. They
are being taken up in a separate tree.

Regression: build clean; smoke-openbios.sh amd64, amd64-fault, amd64-ctx,
amd64-pmem and amd64-linux all PASS.

